[gd_scene load_steps=10 format=3]

; Corporate Shrine — the two delivery platforms (never named) on display
; together, so nobody mistakes them for staff.
;
; The problem this prop solves: the two mascots used to stand loose in the
; dining room at full size, and players read them as two more chibis. A worker
; is a bare toilet at scale_mult 2 (0.90 m tall, 0.63 x 0.95 m). The shrine
; puts the same characters at 0.6 scale — 0.68 m tall, 0.54 x 0.59 m — on a
; plinth behind a rail, with a plaque: the visual language of an ornament.
;
; Native kit units (FurnitureDef.scale_mult = 2 makes them metres):
;   plinth       1.00 x 0.06 x 0.45   the low slab (2.00 x 0.12 x 0.90 m)
;   kerb         0.125 tall x 0.02    front + both sides, on the slab
;   plaque       0.26 x 0.10 x 0.008  brass, tilted 35 deg back on the kerb
;   mascots      0.6 scale, turned inward, centres 0.28 either side of centre
; The whole piece stays inside x 1.00 / z 0.45 and touches the floor (min y 0),
; so it measures 2x1 cells and rotates to 1x2.
;
; The two mascots face EACH OTHER (see the transforms below): a quarter turn
; around Y, +90 deg for the left figure and -90 deg for the right one, so their
; bowls point at the middle of the slab — the two platforms, eye to eye, with
; the plaque between them. A mascot's pivot sits at the back-left corner of its
; mesh (bowl towards +Z, tank at the origin), so the quarter turn swings the
; whole figure sideways: the node origins below are NOT the visual centres, they
; are what puts each centre at x +/-0.28 / z -0.02 — symmetric on the slab,
; bowls 0.27 apart (0.53 m), both clear of the side rails and the back edge.
;
; The mascots are the existing mascot_*.tscn scenes, instanced and scaled:
; their paint (material_override on every mesh *and* the colours baked into the
; meshes' own surface materials) comes along untouched, which is what survives
; the kitchen's tint pass — see the header of mascot_red.tscn. The plinth, kerb
; and plaque are painted the same two-slot way: the colour lives on the BoxMesh
; (the slot _apply_furniture_tints restores) and is repeated as a
; material_override (the slot the drag ghost borrows). Material names are
; shrine_* on purpose: they match no kit material, so a piece tint never
; recolours the display.
;
; Faces +Z, like the kit blueprints: the rail is on the front (+Z) and sides,
; the back is open. The mascots, however, face inwards along X.

